   "evidence": "The PR description says `hes` 'follows from `he` and the inverse identities of `e`'. Constructions.lean:292 declares `(hes : \u2200 q \u2208 e.target, (e.symm q).1 = q.1)`. Parametric.lean:99 calls `e'.slice he' hes' s`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/OpenPartialHomeomorph/Constructions.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `hes` from the signature and derive it inside: for `q \u2208 e.target`, `(e.symm q).1 = (e (e.symm q)).1 = q.1`, using `he _ (e.map_target hq)` and `e.right_inv hq`. Update the four lemmas and the call `e'.slice he' hes' s`, which removes `hes'` from the manifold proof.",
   "issue": "`slice` takes `hes : \u2200 q \u2208 e.target, (e.symm q).1 = q.1`, but this follows from `he` and the inverse laws of `e`. Every consumer has to prove it and pass it in, as `hes'` in Parametric.lean does, and `slice_apply`, `slice_symm_apply`, `mem_slice_source` and `mem_slice_target` all carry it.",
   "line": 292
  }
